Upstream gap: Open WebUI runs image generation and editing on image
connections, each with its own auth type, such as system_oauth, but no
environment variable sets them. Without persistent config, it builds them at
every start from the legacy single-engine settings, which send a static key.

IMAGE_CONNECTIONS holds a JSON array of image connections, in the shape the
IMAGE_CONNECTIONS field of POST /api/v1/images/config/update takes. When no
image connections are stored, startup loads it in place of the legacy
settings, normalized and checked for unique IDs as that route does. An invalid
value stops startup instead of falling back to the legacy defaults, which send
OPENAI_API_KEY to OPENAI_API_BASE_URL. As with other environment settings,
connections that persistent config stores win.

Removal check: an Open WebUI release that sets image connections from the
environment.

